.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.claude/
.hotplate/
node_modules/
dist/
target/
*.log
.env
.env.*

# Flutter/SwiftPM sometimes scaffolds an iOS SourcePackages dir at this level.
implementation/build/

# Visual-parity harness run artefacts (regenerated; bounded to MAX_RUNS_KEPT runs).
/.visual-parity/
.target/

# Python bytecode caches. Nothing in the repo imports its Python tooling as a module —
# every gate runs these files as scripts, and a script run leaves no cache. Investigating
# one interactively does: `sys.path.insert(...)` + `import service_text_reference` to poke
# at a single function is the ordinary way to check a claim about it, and CPython then
# writes a __pycache__ next to the script. That directory is not an artefact of the build
# and must never be committed, whichever session happens to create it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
